  "open_questions": [
    "The 'closed' moment is the first step at full closure; the finger targets slew at <= 2 rad/s, so at that step the joint targets may still lag the closed pose. The 0.5 s hold after it (the close gate) is not recorded.",
    "Normal force per part sums every contact in data.contact; a contact inside the margin with no active constraint has zero force, so B3's 'touching' (a contact exists) and a force > 0 can differ.",
    "Not measured: why 5 of the 50 trials (trials [34, 38, 44, 45, 49]) knocked the cup during the approach, before any finger closed (Run 1: 0). Their cup positions and reasons are in fifty.failed_trials. On the same layouts M1's cylinder (legacy offset) succeeded in 5/5. mug_v1 moves the palm target (L1: approach direction 39.95 instead of 35.54 deg in the palm frame) and changes the contact model; which of these matters was not tested (no more fixes in this track)."
